# Vulnerabilities this repository has decided not to act on, one per line.
#
# An entry silences a finding for everyone until it is removed, so each one
# carries three things, and an entry without them should be deleted:
#
#   1. the CVE id       what is silenced
#   2. why              a reason a reviewer can disagree with: why the code is
#                       unreachable, or why the risk is accepted. Not "false
#                       positive".
#   3. an expiry date   when someone must look again
#
# Format:
#
#   # CVE-2025-00000  expires 2026-12-31
#   # Reached only by <thing this project does not do>. Re-check when <event>.
#   CVE-2025-00000
#
# Not for a CVE with no released fix: the workflow passes --ignore-unfixed, so
# those never fail the build. A CVE that is inconvenient to fix needs a
# dependency bump instead.
#
# The file is empty, and that is its normal state. An entry that stays for long
# usually means an upgrade is due.
